 ## Invariants
 
+- Live BTW snapshot assembly stays inside this adapter because it reads native message and instruction-entry records.
+- The BTW coordinator plugin owns root reservations, head publication and prefix capture through `LIVE_BTW_RPC`.
+- Native fork, import, active-state reads and transcript-only revert use the official SDK here.
+- Prior-side reads start at the tail and stop at the inherited boundary.
+- A fresh main fork provides the immutable snapshot used by the native import route.
+- Import preserves every main message's content and native provider data.
+- A running main assistant becomes a settled reference copy without executing its pending work.
+- Session instruction entries also move to the import before its first prompt.
+- Earlier side turns retain user input, attached context and final assistant text.
+- Earlier side reasoning and tool calls do not enter the rebuilt request.
+- Every earlier question keeps its original main-session premise.
+- A failed authoritative read stops preparation and preserves the previous live transcript.
+
 - `getSessionMessage` reads only the requested session. Pins, message references
